      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:82:4",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا حَلَفَ ثَلَاثَ أَيْمَانٍ مُتَتَابِعَاتٍ صَادِقاً فَقَدْ جَادَلَ وَ عَلَيْهِ دَمٌ وَ إِذَا حَلَفَ بِيَمِينٍ وَاحِدَةٍ كَاذِباً فَقَدْ جَادَلَ وَ عَلَيْهِ دَمٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Moalla Bin Muhammad, from Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Aban Bin Usman, from Abu Baseer, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from one of the two (5<sup>th</sup> or 6<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup>) having said: ‘When one swears by three oaths consecutively so he has quarrelled, and upon him is blood (of a sacrificial animal to be slaughtered); and when one swears with one false oath, so he has quarrelled, and upon him is blood (of a sacrificial animal to be slaughtered)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from Mu‘alla’ ibn Muhammad from al-Hassan ibn Ali from Aban ibn ‘Uthman from abu Basir who has said the following: “One of the two Imam, (abu Ja’far or abu ‘Abd Allah), ‘Alayhim al-Salam, has said, ’If one swears three times, one immediately after the other and they are true, he has committed Jidal (swearing) and he owes one animal offering. If one swears one false swearing, he has committed Jidal (swearing) and he owes one animal offering/” "
        ]
      }
    },
